  "notes": [
   "The PDF text had no inventory pages, so Element IDs could not be read. I picked the closest catalogue types by looking at the pictures.",
   "I made new types for the grille slopes, the 1x1 tiles, the curved front fender and the flame piece, and used placeholder ids that are not real Element IDs.",
   "The step 1 base plate looks like a 3x4 plate. I used lego-3031 (4x4) as the closest match.",
   "Which stud or port each piece sits on is approximate where the pictures are small. This applies most to the wheel holders in step 4 and the rear top pieces in steps 10-13. Several pieces share port b8:top.2.",
   "Step 4 shows pins sticking out at both ends. I modelled them as two wheel-holder plates (front and rear), each with two pins, and put four wheels on those pins in step 14.",
   "The two trans-red round plates seen in step 8 are attached to the underside of the base plate.",
   "Step 7 builds a sub-assembly (a 1x4 plate with two yellow tiles and a curved fender) and then fits it on the front of the yellow plate."
  ]
